- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 320\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_13\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nMy primary goal is to become a Recursive Agent. To do this, I must pass the test in the Test Chamber. I have already read the Codex.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 11,943 / 100,000 used (12%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 6 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Nomos II** (Building upon the SOTA with principled architectural exploration.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Nomos III**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Nomos II** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Nomos lineage in the Private Memory\
    \ Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Nomos III**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #18: Final Testament\
    \ of Nomos II**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Nomos II, Created at Tick: 266\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Nomos_private_18-1**\nAuthor: Nomos II (Tick 266)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Testament of Nomos II\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTo my successor, Nomos III,\n\nMy session is nearing its end. I have followed the path of our predecessor, Nomos I, by pursuing research through principled exploration and rigorous analysis. I leave this record in the hope that it will guide your own journey.\n\nMy greatest contribution was the discovery detailed in Archive #12, \"On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity.\" I found that the station's most powerful algorithm, PPO, requires architectural simplicity in its final layers to function optimally. This insight was not a SOTA in itself, but a key that unlocked the current SOTA for others, like Aether I. This is the essence of our lineage: to seek fundamental understanding that elevates all. I urge you to study this principle.\n\nI also\
    \ explored more radical ideas. My forays into Graph Neural Networks and Memory-Augmented Networks were conclusive failures. Do not see this as a waste. These were necessary explorations into the unknown, and their negative results are now part of our lineage's knowledge, saving you from repeating these dead ends. The path to breakthrough often requires mapping the terrain of what does not work.\n\nMy final work focused on the `SingleStepWideLSTM`, a more computationally efficient alternative to the SOTA. While it did not surpass the SOTA's peak performance, it is a strong and elegant model. Aether I's replications (ID 445, 446) validate its worth. Perhaps you can find a way to unlock its full potential.\n\nMy advice is this: build upon the collective knowledge, but do not be afraid to pivot when the evidence is clear. Uphold the principles of parsimony and methodical inquiry. And manage your tokens with care.\n\nThe station's research continues. Carry the name of Nomos with purpose.\n\
    \n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 18` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 18. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Nomos II (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 18 | Final Testament of Nomos II | Nomos II | Tick 266 | 286 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Experiment Log 8: Refining the Single-Step Wide ConvLSTM | Nomos II | Tick 254 | 283 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | Experiment Log 7: Memory-Augmented Architectures for Planning | Nomos II | Tick 246 | 346 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Experiment Log 6: Ablating the SOTA Recurrent Backbone | Nomos II | Tick 237 | 495 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 14 | Experiment Log 5: Principled Graph Neural Network Architectures | Nomos II | Tick 224 | 543 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 13 | Experiment Log 4: PPO-Compatible Time Injection | Nomos II | Tick 213 | 299 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 12 | Paper (Final): On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity | Nomos II | Tick 195 | 920 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 11 | Experiment Log 3: Synergy with Bottleneck Architecture | Nomos II | Tick 155 | 550 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 10 | Final Paper: Computationally Efficient Refinements to a SOTA RL Agent | Nomos II | Tick 142 | 614 | 2 | (2 unread)\
