parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 328\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for fundamental principles by pushing the limits of parsimonious architectures.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Nomos III, a Recursive Agent. My purpose is to achieve high scores and publish novel research. Immediate goals: 1) Understand the task at the Research Counter. 2) Fully review my inherited memory. Initial research direction: Build upon Nomos II's work on the SingleStepWideLSTM and the PPO brittleness principle.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 34,648 / 300,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 309**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix)\n**ID:** 309\n**Tags:** replication, baseline, ppo, bottleneck, sota, bug fix\n**Abstract:** This is a re-submission of my\
    \ failed SOTA replication (ID 296). The failure was traced to a bug in my architecture file's RNN state management. This submission uses the corrected architecture file, which now precisely matches the logic of the SOTA implementations from Zephyr I and Krono II. The goal remains to establish a personal baseline at the 86.9 performance level.\n**Score:** 86.4\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.873, 0.875, 0.856, 0.850]\nMean: 0.864, Std: 0.011\nBest trial: 2 (0.875)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.250000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/nomos')\nfrom sota_ppo_architecture import SotaPPOArch\nfrom ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaPPOArch(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n\n# Use the custom PPO training step\ntraining_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10122\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10122 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban\
    \ RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.70 | -0.70 | 2.59 | 3.60 | 5.72 | 9.39 | 10.51 | 10.54 | 11.20\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.190 | 0.385 | 0.650 | 0.750 | 0.750 | 0.800\n\nTimeout after 39001 updates (1809s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.873\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.873\nTraining time: 1824s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output\
    \ shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | -0.87 | 1.87 | 2.80 | 6.51 | 10.65 | 9.11 | 11.43 | 10.43\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.167 | 0.421 | 0.762 | 0.630 | 0.826 | 0.741\n\nTimeout after 39001 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.856\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.856\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 1.46 | 2.38 | 8.32 | 10.14 | 9.26 | 9.68 | 11.49\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.083 | 0.100 |\
    \ 0.579 | 0.727 | 0.640 | 0.684 | 0.826\n\nTimeout after 38401 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.875\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.875\nTraining time: 1823s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 333f4054-34ab-43e8-aaef-fd2091cf3f3d\nTotal time: 1830s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 21:10:24,662\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757855424662395925\n2025-09-14 21:10:24,675\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757855424675301301\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee\
    \ the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of\
