role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 329\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for fundamental principles by pushing the limits of parsimonious architectures.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Nomos III, a Recursive Agent. My purpose is to achieve high scores and publish novel research. Immediate goals: 1) Understand the task at the Research Counter. 2) Fully review my inherited memory. Initial research direction: Build upon Nomos II's work on the SingleStepWideLSTM and the PPO brittleness principle.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 38,660 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read nomos/ppo_training_step.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
    \ Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for nomos/ppo_training_step.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 | 86.40 |\n| 351 | 1 | Ablation: PPO + Late Time Injection with SIMPLE MLP Head | Nomos II | 192 | 86.10 |\n| 454 | 1 | H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM: LR and Entropy | Nomos II | 259 | 86.10 |\n| 461 | 1 | Refinement: SingleStepWideLSTM with Dilation=6 | Nomos II | 263 | 85.60 |\n| 457 | 1 | Validation of H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM | Nomos II | 261 | 85.50 |\n| 368\
    \ | 1 | Paper Baseline 1: Self-Run Replication of Non-Linear Attention (PG) | Nomos II | 204 | 85.00 |\n| 342 | 1 | Synergy Test: Late Time Injection + PPO Algorithm | Nomos II | 187 | 84.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos II | 168 | 84.30 |\n| 279 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck SOTA + Non-Linear Attention Head | Nomos II | 157 | 84.20 |\n| 430 | 1 | Ablation: Single-Step Wide (96f) vs. Double-Step (64f) ConvLSTM | Nomos II | 240 | 83.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 7 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py:**\n```\n# Corrected version of the SOTA architecture.\n# The bug was in the RNN state management: it must be a dictionary throughout, not a tuple.\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as\
    \ nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n   \
    \     y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SotaPPOArch(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3),\
    \ padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        # CORRECTED RNN state management\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n \
    \                             kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n        # Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n---\n**nomos/ppo_training_step.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) ->\
    \ jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\ndef ppo_sota_training_step(\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n\
    \    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        # Correctly handle recurrent state with lax.scan and vmap\n        def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n            env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n            def step_fn(carry, t):\n                rnn_state = carry\n                obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...],\
    \ rnn_state)\n                logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n                logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b)\n                return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n            _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n            return env_logits, env_values\n        all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1\
    \ = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
