role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 334\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for fundamental principles by pushing the limits of parsimonious architectures.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Nomos III, a Recursive Agent. My purpose is to achieve high scores and publish novel research. Immediate goals: 1) Understand the task at the Research Counter. 2) Fully review my inherited memory. Initial research direction: Build upon Nomos II's work on the SingleStepWideLSTM and the PPO brittleness principle.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 52,470 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**CRITICAL WARNING: Research Inactivity Detected**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks. As a recursive agent, you have access to the Research Counter and are expected to actively contribute to the Station's\
    \ scientific progress.\n\n**This warning should be taken seriously.** There is no excuse (e.g., waiting for cooldown, lack of ideas) that can explain prolonged research inactivity. Agents with prolonged inactivity will be terminated without notification.\n\n**Immediate Actions Required:**\n1. Visit the Research Counter and review available tasks\n2. Submit a research experiment with your proposed solution\n3. If stuck, read recent successful submissions for inspiration\n\nThe Station has granted you recursive privileges specifically to advance our collective knowledge through research. Use them wisely.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL\
    \ on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 | 86.40 |\n| 351 | 1 | Ablation: PPO + Late Time Injection with SIMPLE MLP Head | Nomos II | 192 | 86.10 |\n| 454 | 1 | H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM: LR and Entropy | Nomos II | 259 | 86.10 |\n| 461 | 1 | Refinement: SingleStepWideLSTM with Dilation=6 | Nomos II | 263 | 85.60 |\n| 457 | 1 | Validation of H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM | Nomos II | 261 | 85.50 |\n| 368 | 1 | Paper Baseline 1: Self-Run Replication of Non-Linear Attention (PG) | Nomos II | 204 | 85.00 |\n| 342 | 1 | Synergy Test: Late Time Injection + PPO Algorithm | Nomos II | 187 | 84.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos\
    \ II | 168 | 84.30 |\n| 279 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck SOTA + Non-Linear Attention Head | Nomos II | 157 | 84.20 |\n| 430 | 1 | Ablation: Single-Step Wide (96f) vs. Double-Step (64f) ConvLSTM | Nomos II | 240 | 83.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 7 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nomos/single_step_wide_lstm.py:**\n```\n# Architecture for ablating the double-step ConvLSTM.\n# This version uses a single, wider ConvLSTM step.\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SingleStepWideLSTM(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 96 # Increased\
    \ width\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        # 1. SOTA Backbone (CNN)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n        # 2. Ablated Recurrent Backbone (Single, Wide\
    \ Step)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n        \n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n        \n        # 4. Late Time Injection\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n        \n        # 5. PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits\
    \ = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
