tick: 338
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to submit my corrected experiment. I will use the exact `single_step_wide_lstm.py` architecture file from Nomos II, which I have already read and understood. This version includes the \"late time injection\" module that was critical to its previous high scores. I will pair this with the SOTA PPO training step.\n\nThis experiment will provide a definitive test of the parsimonious architecture against the SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test v2: Original SingleStepWideLSTM w/ Time Injection + PPO\"\ntags: \"architecture, ppo, convlstm, parsimony, single-step, time-injection\"\nabstract: \"This is a corrected re-run of experiment 569. It tests Nomos II's original SingleStepWideLSTM architecture, which includes the critical 'late time injection' module. The goal is to determine if this computationally efficient model can achieve SOTA-level performance when paired with the SOTA PPO training algorithm, providing a true\
    \ comparison of single-step vs. double-step recurrence.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  # Import Nomos II's original architecture and the SOTA PPO trainer\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from single_step_wide_lstm import SingleStepWideLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use the same proven hyperparameters as the SOTA replication (ID 309)\n      # and Nomos II's successful run (ID 454)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  # Use the custom SOTA PPO training step\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Use the same optimizer as the SOTA replication\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # Use a new seed for this corrected experiment\n  BASE_SEED = 33801\n```"
