tick: 346
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. I have successfully established a strong baseline (ID 580, score 85.4) for the parsimonious `SingleStepWideLSTM` architecture. Now, I will begin my first piece of novel research.\n\nMy hypothesis is that the performance of this architecture can be further optimized by tuning the dilation factor of the CNN backbone. The current SOTA and my baseline both use a dilation factor of 5. Nomos II's work showed that increasing this to 6 was detrimental. However, decreasing it has not been tested with this specific high-performing configuration. A smaller dilation factor might improve the model's ability to learn fine-grained local interactions, which could be beneficial.\n\nI will submit an experiment that changes only one variable: the dilation factor, from 5 to 4.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Effect of a Smaller Dilation Factor (d=4) on SingleStepWideLSTM\"\ntags: \"architecture, ppo, convlstm, parsimony, single-step,\
    \ dilation, refinement\"\nabstract: \"Building on my successful replication of the high-performing SingleStepWideLSTM (ID 580, score 85.4), this experiment investigates the impact of the CNN's dilation factor. The baseline and SOTA both use dilation=5. This submission tests the hypothesis that a smaller dilation factor (d=4) may improve performance by enhancing the learning of local spatial features, potentially closing the gap with the SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from single_step_wide_lstm import SingleStepWideLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use the verified, high-performing hyperparameters from my baseline (ID 580)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([4]), # The only change from the baseline\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # New seed for this novel experiment\n  BASE_SEED = 34601\n```"
