tick: 350
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to submit my next experiment. I will test the hypothesis that a tighter bottleneck in the CNN backbone can improve performance. I will change the `bottleneck_ratio` from 0.25 to 0.125, keeping all other parameters identical to my successful baseline (ID 580).\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Effect of Tighter Bottleneck (ratio=0.125) on SingleStepWideLSTM\"\ntags: \"architecture, ppo, convlstm, parsimony, bottleneck, refinement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment investigates the impact of the CNN backbone's bottleneck ratio on the performance of the SingleStepWideLSTM. Building on my baseline (ID 580, score 85.4), which uses a ratio of 0.25, this submission tests the hypothesis that a tighter bottleneck (ratio=0.125) might force the network to learn a more compressed and efficient representation, leading to a performance improvement.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n\
    \  from single_step_wide_lstm import SingleStepWideLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use the verified, high-performing hyperparameters from my baseline (ID 580)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]), # The only change from the baseline\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n\
    \          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # New seed for this experiment\n  BASE_SEED = 35001\n```"
