    \ been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 85.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.876, 0.848, 0.848, 0.860]\nMean: 0.858, Std: 0.011\nBest trial: 1 (0.876)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000500\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 96.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.125000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable\
    \ resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 35001 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\
    \ --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.05 | 0.98 | 6.44 | 6.05 | 10.36 | 11.10 | 10.27 | 12.34 | 13.06 | 11.62\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.417 | 0.400 | 0.727 | 0.800 | 0.714 | 0.893 | 0.952 | 0.839\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1525s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.848\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.848\nTraining time: 1541s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.55 | 2.11 | 5.75 | 9.24 | 9.84 | 12.00 | 11.32 | 12.30 | 10.59 | 12.64\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.083 | 0.400 | 0.650 | 0.696 | 0.875 | 0.821 | 0.897 | 0.767 | 0.926\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1536s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.848\n\nSeed 3 completed:\n\
    Solve rate: 0.848\nTraining time: 1552s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.43 | 5.04 | 6.57 | 10.62 | 9.79 | 12.45 | 12.22 | 12.94 | 9.75 | 11.63\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.316 | 0.435 | 0.750 | 0.684 | 0.905 | 0.889 | 0.947 | 0.692 | 0.846\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1578s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.876\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.876\nTraining time: 1594s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M\
    \ | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.80 | 5.60 | 9.78 | 11.27 | 12.18 | 8.33 | 11.99 | 11.99 | 11.62 | 11.45\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.353 | 0.692 | 0.818 | 0.880 | 0.600 | 0.875 | 0.867 | 0.846 | 0.824\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1564s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.860\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.860\nTraining time: 1580s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 2370b6d0-e0a1-472a-a230-a0834d7302e6\nTotal time: 2178s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-17 07:36:58,358\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758065818358675799\n2025-09-17 07:36:58,372\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758065818372087640\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained\
    \ drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the\
    \ maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Hypothesis Test: Effect of Tighter Bottleneck (ratio=0.125) on SingleStepWideLSTM' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 593.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 309 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix) | Nomos II | 172 | 86.40 |\n| 351 | 1 | Ablation: PPO + Late Time Injection with SIMPLE MLP Head | Nomos II | 192 | 86.10 |\n| 454 | 1 | H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM: LR and Entropy | Nomos II | 259 | 86.10 |\n| 593 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Effect of Tighter Bottleneck (ratio=0.125) on SingleStepWideLSTM\
    \ | Nomos III | 350 | 85.80 |\n| 461 | 1 | Refinement: SingleStepWideLSTM with Dilation=6 | Nomos II | 263 | 85.60 |\n| 457 | 1 | Validation of H-Param Sweep on SingleStepWideLSTM | Nomos II | 261 | 85.50 |\n| 580 | 1 | Replication: Nomos II's High-Scoring SingleStepWideLSTM (ID 454) | Nomos III | 343 | 85.40 |\n| 368 | 1 | Paper Baseline 1: Self-Run Replication of Non-Linear Attention (PG) | Nomos II | 204 | 85.00 |\n| 342 | 1 | Synergy Test: Late Time Injection + PPO Algorithm | Nomos II | 187 | 84.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos II | 168 | 84.30 |\n\nPage 1 of 7 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-7, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
