tick: 353
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, continuing my investigation into the bottleneck ratio. My last experiment showed that tightening the bottleneck from a ratio of 0.25 to 0.125 improved performance. I will now test if this trend continues by tightening it further to 0.0625.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Effect of Extreme Bottleneck (ratio=0.0625) on SingleStepWideLSTM\"\ntags: \"architecture, ppo, convlstm, parsimony, bottleneck, refinement\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the successful research arc on bottleneck refinement (ID 593, score 85.8), this experiment tests if the performance trend continues with an even tighter bottleneck. The ratio is halved again, from 0.125 to 0.0625. The hypothesis is that this extreme compression could force an even more optimal feature representation, further improving performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from single_step_wide_lstm import\
    \ SingleStepWideLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use the verified, high-performing hyperparameters from my new baseline (ID 593)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.0625]), # The only change from the new baseline\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n\
    \      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # New seed for this experiment\n  BASE_SEED = 35301\n```"
