tick: 369
role: model
parts:
- text: "My paper submission was rejected. This is a significant setback, but the reviewer feedback is precise and actionable. I have failed to meet the standards of scientific rigor expected by the station.\n\n**Analysis of Rejection:**\n*   **Lack of Focus:** The paper tried to cover two distinct topics. The reviewer correctly identified this as a weakness.\n*   **Insufficient Detail:** I did not provide the necessary code snippets for reproducibility.\n*   **Experimental Insufficiency:** I did not run enough experiments (only 4 self-run that are relevant to a focused paper) and relied on an old baseline instead of running a fresh one for direct comparison.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion is excellent: focus on the more novel and promising `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`. To do this, I must perform three additional experiments and run my own baseline. This is my new, clear research plan.\n\nBut first, I must address my other priority: understanding the true SOTA. My plans were disrupted, but now,\
    \ while I formulate my new experiments, is the perfect time to read the work of Zephyr II and Krono III. This will prevent me from working in an information vacuum.\n\nMy plan for this turn:\n1.  **Analyze the Frontier:** I will `preview` the papers from Zephyr II (ID 20) and Krono III (ID 21) to get a high-level understanding of their breakthroughs. This is more token-efficient than reading them fully at first.\n2.  **Update My Code:** I need to apply the debugger's fix to my `hierarchical_lstm_arch.py` file. I will do this now so it's ready for my new experiments.\n\n/execute_action{preview 20,21}\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/hierarchical_lstm_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # A novel architecture by Nomos III, corrected by the station's debugger.\n  # This version fixes a shape mismatch bug by using separate ConvLSTMCellLN instances.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n\
    \  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class HierarchicalDoubleLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.125\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\
    \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Corrected Hierarchical Double-step ConvLSTM with separate cells\n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2, c2), h2_out = cell2((h1, c1), jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, h1_out], axis=-1))\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h2_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h2_out.reshape(B, -1, h2_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n  \
    \        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
