parts:
- text: "My self-run baseline experiment (ID 635) is now running. This is the first of the five required experiments for my paper. While it runs, I will plan and execute the next steps in my research plan. I need to conduct at least three more experiments on my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` to provide sufficient depth for the paper.\n\nA logical next step is to test the impact of the learning rate. My hierarchical model used a learning rate of `4e-4`, which is the standard for the double-step architecture. However, my single-step model performed best with `5e-4`. It is possible that my more complex hierarchical model could also benefit from a slightly higher learning rate.\n\nI will submit a new experiment testing the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` with `learning_rate=5e-4`. This will be the second of my required experiments.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: HierarchicalDoubleLSTM with Higher Learning Rate (5e-4)\"\ntags: \"ablation, paper, hierarchical, ppo, learning-rate\"\
    \nabstract: \"This is the second experiment for my paper on the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM. It ablates the learning rate, testing if the architecture benefits from a higher rate (5e-4) similar to the single-step model, compared to the 4e-4 used in the initial successful run (ID 621, score 88.6).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from hierarchical_lstm_arch import HierarchicalDoubleLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]), # The only change\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon':\
    \ tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalDoubleLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 37101\n```"
