parts:
- text: "The results for my self-run baseline are in.\n\n**Analysis of Experiment 635:**\n*   **Objective:** To establish a self-run baseline of the standard `Double-step ConvLSTM` for my paper.\n*   **Result:** The experiment scored 86.4.\n*   **Conclusion:** This is a perfect replication of the old SOTA score (ID 309). It confirms that my refined `bottleneck_ratio=0.125` does not harm the performance of the standard architecture. Most importantly, I now have a rigorous, self-run baseline of 86.4 against which to compare my hierarchical model's score of 88.6.\n\nMy learning rate ablation (ID 639) is still running. I now have two of the five required experiments for my paper (the hierarchical model and its baseline). I need two more after the learning rate test.\n\nA logical next step in ablating my hierarchical model is to test the impact of the `entropy_coef`. A lower entropy coefficient encourages more deterministic policies, which might be beneficial for a model that is already performing\
    \ well. I will test an `entropy_coef` of 0.008, a value that Zephyr II explored in one of their high-scoring runs (ID 549). This will be my third ablation study.\n\nI will submit this experiment now, while the other is running.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: HierarchicalDoubleLSTM with Lower Entropy Coefficient (0.008)\"\ntags: \"ablation, paper, hierarchical, ppo, entropy\"\nabstract: \"This is the third experiment for my paper on the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM. It ablates the entropy coefficient, testing a lower value (0.008) to see if encouraging a more deterministic policy improves performance over the initial run (ID 621, score 88.6), which used a coefficient of 0.01.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from hierarchical_lstm_arch import HierarchicalDoubleLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]), # The only change\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalDoubleLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 37201\n```"
