tick: 377
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. My paper has been accepted for publication (Archive #22). I have successfully contributed a significant finding to the station's collective knowledge. The reviewer's feedback is not only positive but provides a perfect, logical next step for my research: test if the hierarchical principle scales to deeper recurrent models.\n\nThe SOTA is a quad-step (4-step) model. My hierarchical concept was proven on a double-step model. The most ambitious and potentially highest-impact experiment I can now run is to apply my hierarchical principle to a quad-step architecture.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A `HierarchicalQuadLSTM`, where the output of each recurrent step is fed into the next, will outperform the standard \"parallel\" `Quad-step` SOTA.\n\nThis is a high-risk, high-reward experiment. It directly challenges the SOTA on its own terms, not by copying it, but by attempting to improve its core principle. This aligns perfectly with the station's mandate for novel research.\n\nMy plan\
    \ is now to design, implement, and test this new architecture.\n\n1.  **Design and Code:** I will first write the code for the `HierarchicalQuadLSTM`. This will be a natural extension of my double-step model.\n2.  **Submit Experiment:** I will then submit this new architecture for evaluation. I will use the hyperparameters from Zephyr II's SOTA as my starting point, as it is the most relevant configuration.\n\nI will start by going to the Research Counter to create the new architecture file.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/hierarchical_quad_lstm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III's attempt to build upon the station SOTA.\n  # Applies the proven hierarchical principle to a quad-step recurrence.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Re-using proven components\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n\
    \          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class HierarchicalQuadLSTM(nn.Module):\n      # Based on Zephyr II's SOTA parameters\n      cnn_features_1:\
    \ int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n\
    \          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Hierarchical Quad-Step ConvLSTM\n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          \n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2, c2), h2_out = cell2((h1, c1), jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, h1_out], axis=-1))\n\n          cell3 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h3, c3), h3_out = cell3((h2, c2), jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, h2_out], axis=-1))\n\n          cell4 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h4, c4), h4_out = cell4((h3, c3), jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, h3_out], axis=-1))\n          \n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h4, 'c': c4}\n\n          # Using Zephyr II's Attention+GAP head\n          tokens = h4_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features)\n\
    \          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h4_out)\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          attn_vec = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', tokens, attn_w)\n          gap_vec = jnp.mean(tokens, axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # Using the SOTA Deeper Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
