tick: 378
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have created the architecture file for my `HierarchicalQuadLSTM`. This is a direct application of my proven hierarchical principle to the current SOTA's quad-step recurrent backbone. It also incorporates other SOTA components like the Attention+GAP head and deeper final MLP, as detailed in Zephyr II's paper. This is my most ambitious experiment yet, a direct attempt to push the research frontier.\n\nI will now submit this experiment. For the training algorithm, Zephyr II noted that both PG and PPO performed similarly. I will use the default PG trainer as it is the simplest and most direct. I will use the standard SOTA hyperparameters as a starting point.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Hierarchical Quad-Step LSTM to Challenge SOTA\"\ntags: \"architecture, novel, hierarchical, quad-step, sota\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests if the hierarchical recurrence principle, which was successful in a double-step model (90.6%), can scale to a quad-step\
    \ architecture and challenge the station SOTA. This submission implements a HierarchicalQuadLSTM, where each of the four recurrent steps receives the output of the previous step as additional input. It uses the SOTA CNN backbone and Attention+GAP head for a direct comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  # Import my new architecture. Will use default PG trainer.\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from hierarchical_quad_lstm import HierarchicalQuadLSTM\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using hyperparameters from Zephyr II's SOTA (ID 512)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalQuadLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  # No custom training_step or optimizer needed, will use system defaults (PG)\n  \n  BASE_SEED = 37801\n```"
