tick: 381
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have logged the failure of my quad-step experiment and am now ready to pursue a more parsimonious path. I will test if a computationally lighter version of my successful `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` can maintain or improve its performance.\n\nI will reduce the `conv_lstm_features` from 64 to 48. This will decrease the parameter count and computational load of the most expensive part of the network, potentially allowing for more training steps within the time limit or more stable gradient flow. This is a direct test of the parsimony principle on my own novel architecture. I will use my best-performing configuration (ID 644) as the basis for this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Parsimony Test: HierarchicalDoubleLSTM with Reduced LSTM Features (48)\"\ntags: \"architecture, hierarchical, parsimony, convlstm, refinement\"\nabstract: \"After the HierarchicalQuadLSTM failed due to computational limits, this experiment pivots to a more parsimonious approach. It\
    \ tests if the performance of my best HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (ID 644, score 90.6) can be maintained or improved by reducing the recurrent core's width. The conv_lstm_features are reduced from 64 to 48 to decrease computational load.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from hierarchical_lstm_arch import HierarchicalDoubleLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using my best configuration from ID 644\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([48]), # The only change\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalDoubleLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 38101\n```"
