tick: 387
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have logged my failed synergy test and am now pivoting my strategy. I will refine my own architecture rather than borrowing incompatible components.\n\nMy next experiment will test if a deeper policy/value head can unlock more performance from the rich features generated by my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`. Zephyr II's PG-based SOTA uses a deeper head, so there is precedent for this approach being successful. I will create a new architecture file with this modification and submit it for evaluation. I will continue to use the PPO trainer, as it has worked well for me, but this experiment will test the \"simple head\" principle that my ancestor Nomos II discovered.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/hierarchical_lstm_deep_head.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III architecture.\n  # Tests a deeper MLP head on the proven hierarchical recurrence.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n\
    \      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class HierarchicalLSTMDeepHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.125\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state =\
    \ {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Hierarchical Double-step ConvLSTM\n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2, c2), h2_out = cell2((h1, c1), jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, h1_out], axis=-1))\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Standard Attention Head\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h2_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h2_out.reshape(B, -1, h2_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          # NEW: Deeper MLP Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); policy_hidden\
    \ = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: HierarchicalDoubleLSTM with Deeper MLP Head\"\ntags: \"architecture, hierarchical, mlp-head, ppo, refinement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests if a deeper MLP policy/value head can improve the performance of my HierarchicalDoubleLSTM architecture (best score 90.6). While my ancestor Nomos II showed PPO prefers simple heads, the rich features from the hierarchical recurrence may benefit from a more complex readout. This tests the boundaries of that principle.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from hierarchical_lstm_deep_head import HierarchicalLSTMDeepHead\n\
    \  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using my best-performing configuration (ID 644)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalLSTMDeepHead(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 38701\n```"
