tick: 390
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have logged my previous experiment and am now ready to implement my new idea for a computationally efficient quad-step model. I will create an architecture that uses residual connections between the LSTM steps instead of concatenation. This `ResidualHierarchicalQuadLSTM` should provide the same benefit of hierarchical information flow without the massive memory overhead that caused my last quad-step attempt to fail.\n\nThis is a direct and principled attempt to bridge the gap to the SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/residual_hierarchical_quad_lstm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III's computationally efficient SOTA contender.\n  # Uses residual connections between LSTM steps instead of concatenation.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4\
    \ * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ResidualHierarchicalQuadLSTM(nn.Module):\n      # Based on Zephyr II's SOTA parameters\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2:\
    \ int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not\
    \ None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Residual Hierarchical Quad-Step ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), h1_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          (h2, c2), h2_out = cell((h1, c1), cnn_out + h1_out)\n          (h3, c3), h3_out = cell((h2, c2), cnn_out + h2_out)\n          (h4, c4), h4_out = cell((h3, c3), cnn_out + h3_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h4, 'c': c4}\n\n          # Using Zephyr II's Attention+GAP head\n          tokens = h4_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h4_out)\n          attn_w = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          attn_vec = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', tokens, attn_w)\n          gap_vec = jnp.mean(tokens, axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\
    \n          # Using the SOTA Deeper Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z); value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Challenge: Residual Hierarchical Quad-Step LSTM\"\ntags: \"architecture, novel, hierarchical, quad-step, residual, sota\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a computationally efficient version of my hierarchical recurrence principle, designed to scale to the SOTA's quad-step depth. Instead of concatenating features between recurrent steps (which failed due to OOM in ID 652), this model uses residual connections (addition). This should provide the benefit of hierarchical information\
    \ flow without the memory explosion, in a direct challenge to the 94.3 SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from residual_hierarchical_quad_lstm import ResidualHierarchicalQuadLSTM\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using hyperparameters from Zephyr II's SOTA (ID 512)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ResidualHierarchicalQuadLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n  \n  BASE_SEED = 39001\n```"
