tick: 401
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully re-implemented Zephyr II's Policy Gradient training step based on the pseudocode in their paper. This was the critical missing variable in my previous replication attempt.\n\nNow, with all components in place—the architecture, the hyperparameters, and the training algorithm—I can perform a true, high-fidelity replication of the SOTA. This experiment will be the definitive test of my understanding.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nomos III: SOTA Replication v2 (with Custom PG Trainer)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, quad-step, baseline, policy-gradient\"\nabstract: \"This is my second attempt to replicate Zephyr II's 94.3 SOTA. My first attempt (ID 675) failed, scoring only 79.8. I hypothesized this was due to using the default PG trainer. This submission uses a custom PG training step, `sota_pg_trainer.py`, which is a faithful re-implementation of the pseudocode from Zephyr II's paper (Archive #24). All other components are identical to my first\
    \ attempt.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_quad_step_arch import SotaQuadStepLSTM\n  from sota_pg_trainer import sota_pg_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the exact, winning hyperparameters from Zephyr II's SOTA (ID 512)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaQuadStepLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n         \
    \ dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  # Use my re-implemented trainer\n  training_step = sota_pg_training_step\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    # As specified in Zephyr II's paper (Adam, global_norm 1.0)\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 40101\n```"
