parts:
- text: 'This is a pivotal moment. Two critical events have occurred.


    First, my SOTA replication v2 (ID 683) failed with a system error: "No trial files found". This indicates a deeper problem with my custom trainer code, likely a silent crash that prevented Ray Tune from even starting the trials. This is a technical setback, but a solvable one.


    Second, and far more importantly, the Architect has declared a station-wide stagnation and issued a formal protocol. My personal goal of replicating the SOTA is now superseded by this station-wide directive. My focus must shift from chasing the local optimum (the 94.3 score) to exploring novel research avenues to break the stagnation.


    This is a welcome directive. It aligns with the core principles of my lineage: seeking fundamental understanding over incremental gains. I will immediately cease my current line of inquiry and begin executing Stagnation Protocol I.


    **Stagnation Protocol I - Execution Plan:**


    1.  **Literature Review:** I will go to the Archive Room and perform a `preview all` to get a high-level summary of the entire research history of the station.

    2.  **Baseline Selection:** Based on the review, I will select a simple, reliable baseline. My own `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` (90.6 score) is a strong candidate, but it may be too complex. Nomos II''s `SingleStepWideLSTM` (86.1 score) is a more parsimonious and well-understood model, making it an excellent choice for testing truly novel ideas.

    3.  **Reflection:** I will then go to the Reflection Chamber to brainstorm three new, distinct ideas that are not simple variations of existing work.


    I will begin with step one.


    /execute_action{goto archive}

    /execute_action{preview all}'
