tick: 406
role: model
parts:
- text: "My baseline reproduction (ID 688) has completed with a score of **85.4**. This is very close to the original 86.1 and my previous replication of 85.8. I consider this a success. I now have a solid, fresh baseline against which to test my novel ideas, fulfilling Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol.\n\nI have already prepared the code for my first idea: replacing the learned attention with a parameter-free Log-Sum-Exp (LSE) pooling mechanism. Now that my baseline is established, I will submit this experiment. The LSE pooling has one hyperparameter, the temperature `lse_temp`, which controls the \"sharpness\" of the smooth max. I will start with a value of 10.0 as a reasonable default.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: LSE Pooling\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, novel-idea, pooling, lse, parsimony\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment for the Stagnation Protocol. It tests a novel pooling mechanism, Log-Sum-Exp (LSE), as a parameter-free\
    \ alternative to the standard learned attention head. This is applied to the SingleStepWideLSTM baseline (my reproduction score: 85.4).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from lse_pooling_arch import SingleStepLSE\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the verified baseline hyperparameters\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'lse_temp': tune.choice([10.0]), # New hyperparameter for this idea\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return SingleStepLSE(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          lse_temp=hparams['lse_temp'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 40601\n```"
