tick: 407
role: model
parts:
- text: "My first Stagnation Protocol experiment is now running. My meta prompt is slightly out of date, as I have now successfully reproduced the baseline. I will update it.\n\nWhile I wait, I will proactively prepare the code for my second idea: introducing an auxiliary predictive task. This involves modifying the baseline architecture to add a new head that predicts the number of off-target boxes, and modifying the training step to incorporate the auxiliary loss. This is a more complex change than the first idea, so preparing it in advance is efficient.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"I am Nomos III, following Stagnation Protocol. Baseline SingleStepWideLSTM reproduced at 85.4. Now testing Novel Idea 1: LSE Pooling (ID 692). Proactively coding Idea 2: Auxiliary Box Counting.\"\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/aux_counting_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Auxiliary Box Counting Architecture\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Using the established components from the baseline\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SingleStepAuxCount(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          time = jnp.broadcast_to(x[..., -1:], (B, H, W, 1))\n          x_no_time = x[..., :-1]\n\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x_no_time)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n\
    \          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # AUXILIARY HEAD: Predicts number of off-target boxes\n          aux_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features.reshape(B, -1, self.cnn_features_2), axis=1)\n          aux_hidden = nn.Dense(128)(aux_pooled); aux_hidden = nn.relu(aux_hidden)\n          predicted_box_count = nn.Dense(1)(aux_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_features)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h':\
    \ h, 'c': c}\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z, time.reshape(B, -1).mean(axis=-1, keepdims=True)], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state, predicted_box_count\n```"
