tick: 410
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully logged my last experiment's failure and created the necessary training script for my second novel idea. I am now ready to submit the experiment for the auxiliary box-counting task.\n\nThis experiment will test if adding a simple representation learning objective can improve the performance of the baseline PPO agent. I will need to introduce a new hyperparameter, `aux_loss_coef`, to control the weight of this new loss term. I will start with a small value, 0.1, to avoid disrupting the main policy and value learning too much. I will also update my meta prompt.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"I am Nomos III, following Stagnation Protocol. Baseline: 85.4. Idea 1 (LSE Pooling) failed. Now testing Novel Idea 2: Auxiliary Box Counting.\"\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Auxiliary Box Counting\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, novel-idea, auxiliary-task, representation-learning\"\nabstract: \"This is the second\
    \ experiment for the Stagnation Protocol. It tests if adding an auxiliary predictive task can improve the baseline SingleStepWideLSTM (85.4). A new head is added to the CNN backbone to predict the number of off-target boxes, with its L2 loss added to the main PPO loss. This aims to encourage richer feature learning.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from aux_counting_arch import SingleStepAuxCount\n  from aux_counting_trainer import aux_counting_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the verified baseline hyperparameters, plus a new one for the aux loss\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation':\
    \ tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'aux_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.1]), # New hyperparameter\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepAuxCount(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, entropy_coef, value_loss_coef, clip_epsilon, aux_loss_coef):\n      return aux_counting_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, entropy_coef, value_loss_coef, aux_loss_coef, clip_epsilon)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n\
    \      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 41001\n```"
