tick: 412
role: model
parts:
- text: "After reviewing my `aux_counting_trainer.py` code, I believe I've spotted the error.\n\nIn the GAE calculation, I copied a version from one of my PPO trainers that includes a hard-coded advantage clipping range: `jnp.clip(advantages, -clip_range, clip_range)`. This is not part of the standard PPO implementation I've been using as a baseline. More importantly, the `clip_range` is not passed into the `loss_fn`, so it is not defined within the JIT-compiled scope, which would cause a crash.\n\nFurthermore, my unpacking of the network outputs is incorrect. The `network.apply` call returns four values, but in my `loss_fn`, I unpack it as `policy_logits, values, _, predicted_box_count`. I am discarding the third return value (the new RNN state), which is bad practice and could potentially cause issues, but the real error is likely the unpacking itself. My baseline PPO trainer's `loss_fn` only takes `params` as an argument. The training function handles the `network.apply` call outside\
    \ the loss function. I have mixed two different patterns. The `network.apply` call should be *inside* the `loss_fn` to be differentiated correctly.\n\nI have made a series of sloppy errors. I will now correct the trainer file, and then resubmit the experiment. I will remove the erroneous advantage clipping and correct the structure of the loss function.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/aux_counting_trainer.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Auxiliary Box Counting Trainer (v2, Corrected)\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict\n\n  # Using a standard GAE implementation, corrected from previous version\n  def gae_advantages(rewards, dones, values, final_value):\n      advantages = jnp.zeros_like(rewards)\n      gae = 0\n      for t in reversed(range(rewards.shape[0])):\n          value_t = values[t]\n          value_tp1 = values[t+1] if t < rewards.shape[0] - 1 else final_value\n          delta\
    \ = rewards[t] + 0.99 * (1 - dones[t]) * value_tp1 - value_t\n          gae = delta + 0.99 * 0.95 * (1 - dones[t]) * gae\n          advantages = advantages.at[t].set(gae)\n      return advantages\n\n  def aux_counting_training_step(network: nn.Module, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch: Dict, entropy_coef: float, value_loss_coef: float, aux_loss_coef: float, clip_epsilon: float):\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Unpack batch\n          obs, actions, rewards, dones, old_log_probs, old_values, final_value = (\n              batch['obs'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones'],\n              batch['log_probs'], batch['values'], batch['final_value']\n          )\n          \n          # Get new network outputs\n          policy_logits, values, new_rnn_state, predicted_box_count = network.apply(params, obs, dones)\n          \n          # Calculate true number of off-target boxes (channel 4 is 'box')\n          true_box_count = jnp.sum(obs[..., 4], axis=(1, 2))\n\
    \n          # GAE Calculation\n          advantages = gae_advantages(rewards, dones, old_values, final_value)\n          returns = advantages + old_values\n          advantages = (advantages - advantages.mean()) / (advantages.std() + 1e-8)\n          \n          # PPO Policy Loss\n          log_probs = nn.log_softmax(policy_logits)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs, actions[..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio = jnp.exp(action_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          pg_loss1 = -advantages * ratio\n          pg_loss2 = -advantages * jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - clip_epsilon, 1.0 + clip_epsilon)\n          policy_loss = jnp.maximum(pg_loss1, pg_loss2).mean()\n          \n          # PPO Value Loss\n          value_pred_clipped = old_values + (values - old_values).clip(-clip_epsilon, clip_epsilon)\n          value_losses = (values - returns) ** 2\n          value_losses_clipped = (value_pred_clipped - returns) ** 2\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.maximum(value_losses,\
    \ value_losses_clipped).mean()\n          \n          # Entropy Loss\n          entropy = -(nn.softmax(policy_logits) * nn.log_softmax(policy_logits)).sum(-1).mean()\n          \n          # AUXILIARY LOSS (L2 distance on box count)\n          aux_loss = 0.5 * ((predicted_box_count - jax.lax.stop_gradient(true_box_count)) ** 2).mean()\n          \n          # Total Loss\n          total_loss = policy_loss + value_loss_coef * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy + aux_loss_coef * aux_loss\n          \n          return total_loss, (policy_loss, value_loss, entropy, aux_loss)\n\n      (loss, (p_loss, v_loss, ent, a_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n      updates, new_opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      new_params = jax.tree_util.tree_map(lambda p, u: p + u, params, updates)\n      \n      return new_params, new_opt_state, (loss, p_loss, v_loss, ent, a_loss)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea\
    \ 2: Auxiliary Box Counting (v2, Corrected)\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, novel-idea, auxiliary-task, representation-learning, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is a corrected resubmission of my second Stagnation Protocol experiment (ID 702), which failed due to a bug in the custom trainer. The trainer code has been corrected. This experiment tests if adding an auxiliary task (predicting the number of off-target boxes) can improve the performance of the SingleStepWideLSTM baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from aux_counting_arch import SingleStepAuxCount\n  from aux_counting_trainer import aux_counting_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'aux_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.1]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepAuxCount(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, entropy_coef, value_loss_coef, clip_epsilon, aux_loss_coef):\n      return aux_counting_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, entropy_coef, value_loss_coef, aux_loss_coef, clip_epsilon)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n  \
    \        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 41201\n```"
