tick: 418
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have created the architecture file for my third and final novel idea. I am hopeful that this simpler architectural change will avoid the bugs that plagued my previous attempt. I will now submit the experiment. This test will determine if allowing the agent to learn when to update its recurrent state can improve performance over the baseline.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Gated State Updates\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, novel-idea, recurrent-memory, gating\"\nabstract: \"This is the third experiment for the Stagnation Protocol. It tests a novel memory management mechanism on the SingleStepWideLSTM baseline (85.4). A learned gate, controlled by the CNN features, determines the extent to which the ConvLSTM's recurrent state is updated at each step. This allows the agent to learn to preserve its long-term memory during less critical state transitions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n\
    \  from gated_update_arch import SingleStepGatedUpdate\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the verified baseline hyperparameters\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepGatedUpdate(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n\
    \      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 41801\n```"
