tick: 423
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. My generalization baseline, the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`, has completed with a score of **90.9** (ID 726). This is consistent with my previous best score of 90.6 and establishes a very strong second baseline for my study.\n\nI have now completed three of the five required experiments for my paper:\n1.  Baseline 1 (`SingleStepWideLSTM`): **85.4** (ID 688)\n2.  Method 1 (Gated `SingleStepWideLSTM`): **83.3** (ID 722)\n3.  Baseline 2 (`HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`): **90.9** (ID 726)\n\nI have already prepared the code for the final two experiments. I will now submit them sequentially. First, the generalization test: applying the gated update to the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`. Second, the ablation test: using the LSTM state as the gating signal on the `SingleStepWideLSTM`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Update Study, Exp 4: Generalization Test (Gated HierarchicalDoubleLSTM)\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, generalization, hierarchical, gating\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"This is the fourth experiment in my 5-part study. It serves as the generalization test for the Gated State Update mechanism. The gating mechanism is applied to my high-performing HierarchicalDoubleLSTM architecture (baseline score: 90.9) to see if the (negative) effect is consistent across a second, distinct, and more complex architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from gated_hierarchical_arch import GatedHierarchicalDoubleLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the verified baseline hyperparameters for this architecture\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return GatedHierarchicalDoubleLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42301\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Update Study, Exp 5: Ablation (LSTM-State Gate)\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, ablation, gating, recurrent-memory\"\nabstract: \"This is the fifth and final experiment\
    \ in my 5-part study on Gated State Updates. This is an ablation test on the SingleStepWideLSTM baseline (85.4). Instead of deriving the gate signal from the CNN features (perception), this version derives it from the previous LSTM hidden state (memory). This tests the importance of the gating signal's source.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from gated_update_ablation_arch import SingleStepGatedUpdateAblation\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the verified baseline hyperparameters for this architecture\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n\
    \          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepGatedUpdateAblation(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42302\n```"
