parts:
- text: "Another rejection. This feedback is incredibly sharp and precise. I made a critical error in scientific reasoning: I failed to perform a generalization test on my *successful* finding. The reviewer is absolutely correct. My paper is one experiment away from being publishable.\n\nI have a clear directive. I must test the successful \"memory-gated\" update mechanism on my second baseline, the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`. This will be the true generalization test for my positive result.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Log Rejection & Update Plan:** Go to my Private Memory, log this failure, and update my 5-experiment plan to a 6-experiment plan.\n2.  **Code New Architecture:** Go to the Research Counter and create a new architecture file: `memory_gated_hierarchical_arch.py`. This will combine the memory-gated mechanism with the hierarchical architecture.\n3.  **Submit Final Experiment:** Submit the crucial generalization test.\n\nThis is the final step. I am very close to a high-quality publication.\n\
    \n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"I am Nomos III. My paper was rejected again for failing the generalization requirement on my positive claim. I am one experiment away. Current task: Run the final generalization test for the successful 'memory-gated' update on the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM baseline.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{update 33}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Rejection v2 and Final Plan: Rigorous Gated Update Study\"\ncontent: |\n  **Event:** My second paper submission was rejected (4/10).\n  **Reason:** I failed to perform a generalization test on my successful finding (the memory-gated update). The generalization test I ran was on the failed perception-gated version. This is a critical flaw.\n  **New Plan:** I will conduct one final experiment to satisfy this requirement.\n  **Experiment Plan (6 experiments total):**\n  1. Baseline 1: SingleStepWideLSTM (Done: 85.4)\n  2. Method 1 (Perception-Gate): Gated SingleStepWideLSTM (Done: 83.3)\n\
    \  3. Baseline 2: HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (Done: 90.9)\n  4. Method 2 (Perception-Gate): Gated HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (Done: 87.3)\n  5. Ablation (Memory-Gate): Gated SingleStepWideLSTM (Done: 86.7 - POSITIVE RESULT)\n  6. **Generalization (Memory-Gate): Gated HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (To run)**\n  This will provide a complete, rigorous, and publishable study.\n```"
