tick: 427
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan is updated and my course is clear. I will now create the architecture file for the final, critical experiment and submit it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/memory_gated_hierarchical_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Gated Update Study, Exp 6: Memory-Gated HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (Generalization)\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o\
    \ * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.125\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out\
    \ = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Memory-Gated Hierarchical Double-step ConvLSTM\n          # Gate 1 is based on the initial hidden state\n          gate1_features = jnp.mean(rnn_state['h'].reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          gate1_hidden = nn.Dense(32)(gate1_features);\
    \ gate1_hidden = nn.relu(gate1_hidden)\n          gate1_sigmoid = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(gate1_hidden)).reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n\n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1_updated, c1_updated), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_features)\n          \n          h1_new = (1 - gate1_sigmoid) * rnn_state['h'] + gate1_sigmoid * h1_updated\n          c1_new = (1 - gate1_sigmoid) * rnn_state['c'] + gate1_sigmoid * c1_updated\n\n          # Gate 2 is based on the state after step 1\n          gate2_features = jnp.mean(h1_new.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          gate2_hidden = nn.Dense(32)(gate2_features); gate2_hidden = nn.relu(gate2_hidden)\n          gate2_sigmoid = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(gate2_hidden)).reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n\n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2_updated, c2_updated), h2_out = cell2((h1_new, c1_new), jnp.concatenate([cnn_features, h1_out], axis=-1))\n          \n      \
    \    h2_new = (1 - gate2_sigmoid) * h1_new + gate2_sigmoid * h2_updated\n          c2_new = (1 - gate2_sigmoid) * c1_new + gate2_sigmoid * c2_updated\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2_new, 'c': c2_new}\n\n          z = jnp.mean(h2_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Update Study, Exp 6: Generalization of Positive Result\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, generalization, hierarchical, gating, memory-gate\"\nabstract: \"This is the sixth and final experiment in my study of Gated Recurrent Updates, designed to satisfy the generalization requirement for my one positive finding. This experiment applies the successful 'memory-gated' update mechanism (which scored 86.7% on the SingleStepWideLSTM) to my second, more complex baseline,\
    \ the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM (baseline score: 90.9%). This will determine if the small performance gain generalizes or is context-dependent.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from memory_gated_hierarchical_arch import MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42701\n```"
