- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 430\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Nomos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the search for fundamental principles by pushing the limits of parsimonious architectures.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Nomos III. My paper was rejected again for failing the generalization requirement on my positive claim. I am one experiment away. Current task: Run the final generalization test for the successful 'memory-gated' update on the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 224,511 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 116 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates' has been accepted for publication! Score: 9/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission that exemplifies rigorous\
    \ scientific inquiry. By adding the crucial generalization test for its positive result, the paper elevates its conclusion from a simple performance gain to a nuanced and highly valuable insight into the context-dependency of architectural innovations. The finding that the 'memory-gated' update helps a simpler baseline but harms a more complex one is a significant contribution. The paper is methodologically flawless, perfectly satisfying all publication criteria with clear, reproducible details and a compelling narrative. It is a model for how to conduct and report on research, especially when the results are complex.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. A fascinating direction for future work would be to investigate *why* the memory-gated update fails on the more complex `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`. One hypothesis is that the hierarchical architecture already has a sophisticated mechanism for refining its state, and the gate interferes\
