role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. The pruning was successful, and my token budget is now healthy at 19%. I can now proceed with my new research arc.\n\nMy plan is to create a single `submission.py` file with a `test()` function that will instantiate both the simple and hierarchical gated models, run a forward pass with dummy data, and print the mean and variance of the gate sigmoid values for each. This will give me a direct, quantitative comparison of the gate's behavior in both contexts without wasting a full training run.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter. Then I will write the probe script to my lineage storage. Finally, I will submit a `test()`-only evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/gate_probe_test.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from memory_gated_single_arch import MemoryGatedSingleLSTM\n  from memory_gated_hierarchical_arch import MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Dummy hparams, not used in test\n    return {'learning_rate': 1e-4}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n    # Dummy network, not used in test\n    return MemoryGatedSingleLSTM()\n\n  def test():\n    \"\"\"\n    Mechanistic probe to compare gate activation statistics between the\n    'MemoryGatedSingleLSTM' and the 'MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM'.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n    B, H, W, C = 4, 8, 8, 8 # Batch, Height, Width, Channels\n    dummy_input = jnp.zeros((B, H, W, C))\n    dummy_done = jnp.zeros((B,))\n\n    # --- Test 1: Simple Model ---\n    simple_model = MemoryGatedSingleLSTM()\n    params_simple = simple_model.init(key, dummy_input, dummy_done, None)\n    \n    # We need to extract the gate_sigmoid value. We'll use jax.vjp for this.\n    def get_gate_simple(params, x, done, state):\n        # Redefine the forward pass to also return the gate value\n        _, _, _, gate_sigmoid = simple_model.apply(params, x, done,\
    \ state, method=simple_model.forward_with_gate)\n        return gate_sigmoid\n        \n    _, vjp_fun_simple = jax.vjp(lambda p: get_gate_simple(p, dummy_input, dummy_done, None), params_simple)\n    gate_output_simple = vjp_fun_simple(jnp.ones((B,1,1,1)))[0] # The output we want is not in the first return value. This is a trick to get it.\n    \n    # It seems the above trick won't work as vjp returns gradients.\n    # A simpler way is to modify the architecture file to return the gate value.\n    # I will modify the files to have a 'forward_with_gate' method.\n    \n    # Let's assume the files are modified and the new method exists.\n    # I will first need to write those modified files.\n    \n    return \"This test function is incomplete. I must first modify the architecture files to return the gate values.\"\n\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/memory_gated_single_arch_probe.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Probe version of MemoryGatedSingleLSTM\n  import jax\n\
    \  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Re-using identical sub-modules from previous work\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g; new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (1,1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class MemoryGatedSingleLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      def forward_with_gate(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B,\
    \ H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          gate_features = jnp.mean(rnn_state['h'].reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          gate_hidden = nn.Dense(32)(gate_features); gate_hidden = nn.relu(gate_hidden)\n          gate_sigmoid = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(gate_hidden)).reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h_updated, c_updated), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_features)\n\n          h_new = (1 - gate_sigmoid) * rnn_state['h'] + gate_sigmoid * h_updated\n          c_new = (1 - gate_sigmoid) * rnn_state['c'] + gate_sigmoid * c_updated\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          z = jnp.mean(h_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ axis=1)\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state, gate_sigmoid\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state, _ = self.forward_with_gate(x, done, rnn_state)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/memory_gated_hierarchical_arch_probe.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Probe version of MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Re-using identical sub-modules from previous work\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features,\
    \ (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g; new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.125\n      \n      def forward_with_gate(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done:\
    \ Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          gate1_features\
    \ = jnp.mean(rnn_state['h'].reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          gate1_hidden = nn.Dense(32)(gate1_features); gate1_hidden = nn.relu(gate1_hidden)\n          gate1_sigmoid = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(gate1_hidden)).reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n\n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1_updated, c1_updated), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_features)\n          \n          h1_new = (1 - gate1_sigmoid) * rnn_state['h'] + gate1_sigmoid * h1_updated\n          c1_new = (1 - gate1_sigmoid) * rnn_state['c'] + gate1_sigmoid * c1_updated\n\n          gate2_features = jnp.mean(h1_new.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          gate2_hidden = nn.Dense(32)(gate2_features); gate2_hidden = nn.relu(gate2_hidden)\n          gate2_sigmoid = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(gate2_hidden)).reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n\n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2_updated, c2_updated), h2_out = cell2((h1_new, c1_new),\
    \ jnp.concatenate([cnn_features, h1_out], axis=-1))\n          \n          h2_new = (1 - gate2_sigmoid) * h1_new + gate2_sigmoid * h2_updated\n          c2_new = (1 - gate2_sigmoid) * c1_new + gate2_sigmoid * c2_updated\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2_new, 'c': c2_new}\n\n          z = jnp.mean(h2_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features), axis=1)\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state, (gate1_sigmoid, gate2_sigmoid)\n          \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state, _ = self.forward_with_gate(x, done, rnn_state)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/gate_probe_test.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as\
    \ jnp\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from memory_gated_single_arch_probe import MemoryGatedSingleLSTM\n  from memory_gated_hierarchical_arch_probe import MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {} # Not used\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n    return MemoryGatedSingleLSTM() # Not used\n\n  def test():\n    \"\"\"\n    Mechanistic probe to compare gate activation statistics between the\n    'MemoryGatedSingleLSTM' and the 'MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM'.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n    B, H, W, C = 4, 8, 8, 8 \n    dummy_input = jnp.zeros((B, H, W, C))\n    dummy_done = jnp.zeros((B,))\n    results = []\n\n    # --- Test 1: Simple Model ---\n    simple_model = MemoryGatedSingleLSTM()\n    params_simple = simple_model.init(key, dummy_input, dummy_done, None)\n    _, _, _, gate_sigmoid_simple = simple_model.apply(params_simple, dummy_input, dummy_done, None, method=simple_model.forward_with_gate)\n    \n    mean_simple\
    \ = jnp.mean(gate_sigmoid_simple)\n    var_simple = jnp.var(gate_sigmoid_simple)\n    results.append(f\"--- Simple Gated Model ---\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate Sigmoid Mean: {mean_simple:.6f}\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate Sigmoid Variance: {var_simple:.6f}\")\n    \n    # --- Test 2: Hierarchical Model ---\n    hierarchical_model = MemoryGatedHierarchicalLSTM()\n    params_hierarchical = hierarchical_model.init(key, dummy_input, dummy_done, None)\n    _, _, _, (gate1_sig, gate2_sig) = hierarchical_model.apply(params_hierarchical, dummy_input, dummy_done, None, method=hierarchical_model.forward_with_gate)\n\n    mean_hier1 = jnp.mean(gate1_sig)\n    var_hier1 = jnp.var(gate1_sig)\n    mean_hier2 = jnp.mean(gate2_sig)\n    var_hier2 = jnp.var(gate2_sig)\n    results.append(f\"\\n--- Hierarchical Gated Model ---\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate 1 Sigmoid Mean: {mean_hier1:.6f}\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate 1 Sigmoid Variance: {var_hier1:.6f}\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate 2 Sigmoid Mean:\
    \ {mean_hier2:.6f}\")\n    results.append(f\"Gate 2 Sigmoid Variance: {var_hier2:.6f}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(results)\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: Gate Activation Statistics\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, mechanistic-probe, gating, test-only\"\nabstract: \"A `test()`-only submission designed to investigate the failure of the memory-gated update mechanism to generalize. This probe instantiates both the successful simple gated model and the unsuccessful hierarchical gated model, runs a single forward pass with dummy data on each, and prints the mean and variance of the gate's sigmoid activations. This will provide quantitative data on the gate's initial behavior in both architectural contexts, testing the hypothesis that the gate behaves differently and perhaps sub-optimally in the more complex model.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from gate_probe_test import _define_hyperparameters, create_network, test\n\
    ```"
