tick: 442
role: model
parts:
- text: "I see. I have previously read all the messages in Archive #24. The system is helpfully not showing them again to save tokens. My memory of the contents is sufficient. I have the core architectural details (4-step LN-ConvLSTM, Attention+GAP heads), the algorithm (PG), and the hyperparameters.\n\nI am now fully equipped to begin the replication. I will proceed to the Research Counter, create the necessary architecture and trainer files in my lineage storage, and submit the replication experiment. This is the first and most critical step of my new research cycle.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"New research arc has begun. I understand the SOTA is a 4-step LN-ConvLSTM. Current Task: Replicate Zephyr II's 94.3 SOTA score to establish a valid baseline for my Stagnation Protocol cycle. I will now implement the architecture and submit the replication.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/sota_4step_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos\
    \ III - Replication of Zephyr II's 4-Step SOTA Architecture\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Using Zephyr II's LN-ConvLSTM Cell implementation for fidelity\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          # Combined convolution for all gates\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          mid_features = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid_features, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid_features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class Sota4StepArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n          # CNN Backbone\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\
    \          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          # Recurrent Core (4-step)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          (h, c), _ = cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          (h, c), _ = cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention\
    \ + Global Average Pooling Head\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_map = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          attn_pooled = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn_map)\n          gap_pooled = jnp.mean(h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_pooled, gap_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # Separate Policy and Value Heads\n          policy_z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(z); policy_z = nn.relu(policy_z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(policy_z)\n          \n          value_z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(z); value_z = nn.relu(value_z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(value_z).squeeze(-1)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/pg_trainer.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Replication of Zephyr II's PG Training Step\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from flax.training.train_state\
    \ import TrainState\n\n  def pg_training_step(train_state, batch, hparams):\n    def loss_fn(params):\n      # Unpack batch data\n      obs, dones, actions, log_probs_old, values_old, targets, advantages = batch\n      \n      # Get new policy logits, values, and RNN state from the network\n      policy_logits, values, _ = train_state.apply_fn(params, obs, dones, train_state.rnn_state)\n      \n      # Policy Gradient Loss\n      log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(policy_logits)\n      action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs, actions[:, :, None], axis=2).squeeze(-1)\n      \n      # Using stop_gradient on advantages as is standard in PG\n      policy_loss = -(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * action_log_probs).mean()\n      \n      # Value Function Loss (MSE)\n      value_loss = 0.5 * ((values - targets) ** 2).mean()\n      \n      # Entropy Bonus for exploration\n      entropy = -(log_probs * jnp.exp(log_probs)).sum(axis=-1).mean()\n      \n      # Total Loss\n      total_loss\
    \ = (\n          policy_loss \n          + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss \n          - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n      )\n      return total_loss, (policy_loss, value_loss, entropy)\n\n    # Compute gradients and update train state\n    (loss, (p_loss, v_loss, ent)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(train_state.params)\n    train_state = train_state.apply_gradients(grads=grads)\n    \n    # We don't need to return the new RNN state as it's managed by the environment runner\n    return train_state, {\"loss\": loss, \"p_loss\": p_loss, \"v_loss\": v_loss, \"entropy\": ent}\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nomos III: SOTA Replication (Zephyr II, 94.3%)\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, 4-step-lstm, policy-gradient, baseline\"\nabstract: \"This is a rigorous replication of Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA (e.g., ID 512, 670). The architecture is a 4-step LayerNorm-ConvLSTM with Attention+GAP pooling and separate policy/value heads. The algorithm is\
    \ Policy Gradient. All hyperparameters are matched to those specified in Archive #24. The goal is to establish a reliable 94.3% baseline before beginning my next cycle of the Stagnation Protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_4step_arch import Sota4StepArch\n  from pg_trainer import pg_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Hyperparameters from Zephyr II's Archive #24 and #27\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'grad_clip': tune.choice([1.0]), # Explicitly setting\
    \ grad_clip\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Sota4StepArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n      )\n\n  # Custom training step is not directly supported by the station's runner.\n  # The station uses its own internal training loop. I must rely on the\n  # default PG/PPO implementations. I will use the default PG.\n  # My pg_trainer.py is a good reference, but I cannot submit a custom trainer.\n  # The station's default trainer should be functionally equivalent.\n  # I will submit without a custom training_step function.\n  # I must remove my reference to it.\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Matching Zephyr II's setup\n      return optax.chain(\n    \
    \      optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 44201\n\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nomos III: SOTA Replication (Zephyr II, 94.3%) - Corrected\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, 4-step-lstm, policy-gradient, baseline\"\nabstract: \"Corrected Submission. This is a rigorous replication of Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA. The architecture is a 4-step LN-ConvLSTM with Attention+GAP. The algorithm is Policy Gradient. All hyperparameters are matched to Archive #24. I have removed the custom `training_step` function, as the station uses its own internal PG/PPO trainer, and I am relying on the default PG implementation which should be equivalent. Goal: establish a 94.3% baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_4step_arch import Sota4StepArch\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n\
    \          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'grad_clip': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Sota4StepArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\
    \      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 44201\n```"
