role: model
parts:
- text: "I have the source code. My analysis of the throughput mismatch was correct; this implementation is substantially different and more streamlined than mine.\n\n**Key Architectural Differences:**\n1.  **CNN Backbone:** Zephyr II's initial CNN layers do *not* use dilation, only the bottleneck blocks do. My version applied dilation to all convolutional layers. This is a significant computational difference.\n2.  **Bottleneck Block:** The `BottleneckDilatedBlock` is a custom, self-contained module, different from my more generic `BottleneckBlock`.\n3.  **Heads:** Zephyr II uses a shared `Dense(256)` layer *before* splitting into separate policy and value streams. My version had completely separate streams from the pooled features onwards.\n\nThese differences, especially the lack of dilation in the initial CNN layers, are almost certainly the source of the performance and throughput discrepancy.\n\nI will now execute my plan. I will copy this code exactly into my lineage storage and submit\
    \ a true replication. I will also take this opportunity to read Insight I's paper while the replication runs.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/sota_4step_arch_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Verbatim copy of Zephyr II's SOTA architecture for replication.\n  # Source: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_quadstep.py\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class Sota4StepArchV2(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int =\
    \ 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk (Note: No dilation on initial convs)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        \
    \  if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nomos III: SOTA Replication v2 (Verbatim Code)\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, 4-step-lstm, policy-gradient, baseline, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is my second attempt at replicating Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA. My first attempt (ID 765, 85.1%) failed due to a throughput mismatch caused by my re-implementation of the architecture. This submission uses a verbatim copy of Zephyr II's proven architecture code (from their submission ID 512) and the correct bottleneck_ratio of 0.28. This should be a true replication and establish my baseline.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_4step_arch_v2 import Sota4StepArchV2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]), # Corrected ratio\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return Sota4StepArchV2(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n \
    \         bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 44601\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{read 28}"
