tick: 448
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success. My verbatim SOTA replication (ID 773) scored **93.4**. This is well within the stochastic variance of Zephyr II's 94.3 SOTA. Crucially, the logs show that my runs completed the full 39,062 updates, confirming that the throughput issue is resolved. I have now successfully established my baseline.\n\nThe reproducibility crisis is over. I have a solid, high-performing foundation upon which to build.\n\nMy reflection session has already provided me with three promising, throughput-neutral hypotheses. I will begin testing the first one: **Dynamic Bottleneck Ratio**. This is the most novel and ambitious of the three ideas. I will create a new architecture file that implements this concept and submit it for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"SOTA replication successful (93.4 vs 94.3). Throughput issue is solved. I now have a valid baseline. My new research cycle begins now, testing the three throughput-neutral ideas I developed. First up: Dynamic Bottleneck\
    \ Ratio.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/dynamic_bottleneck_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Dynamic Bottleneck Ratio\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Using the verified SOTA components\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      # Ratio is now passed during the call\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, bottleneck_ratio: float):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class DynamicBottleneckArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Ratio Controller Network\n          # Predicts a bottleneck ratio between 0.1 and 0.5 based on the global state\n          # This is extremely lightweight\n          controller_input\
    \ = jnp.mean(x.reshape(B, -1), axis=1)\n          ratio_hidden = nn.Dense(16)(controller_input); ratio_hidden = nn.relu(ratio_hidden)\n          # Sigmoid maps to (0,1), scale and shift to get (0.1, 0.5)\n          predicted_ratio = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(1)(ratio_hidden)).squeeze(-1) * 0.4 + 0.1\n          \n          # CNN trunk with dynamic ratio\n          # We must pass the ratio as a static argument for jax.jit.\n          # A pure dynamic ratio is not feasible.\n          # ALTERNATIVE IMPLEMENTATION: Gated Blending of two fixed bottlenecks\n          # This is throughput-neutral and jit-compatible.\n          \n          # This dynamic ratio idea is more complex than anticipated due to jit.\n          # I will pivot to my second idea, which is simpler and safer to implement:\n          # Time-Aware Policy Head. I will implement that instead.\n          # I must create a new file.\n          pass # This file is now abandoned.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/time_aware_head_arch.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Time-Aware Policy Head\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Using verbatim SOTA components\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n\
    \          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i=nn.sigmoid(i); f=nn.sigmoid(f); o=nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class TimeAwareSotaArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          time_feature = x[:, 0, 0, 7:8] # Extract time feature (constant across spatial dims)\n\n          # CNN trunk (Verbatim from SOTA)\n          cnn_body = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); cnn_body = nn.relu(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio,\
    \ self.dilation)(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(cnn_body); cnn_body = nn.relu(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(cnn_body)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), cnn_body)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits,\
    \ axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          \n          # MODIFICATION: Inject time feature before the heads\n          z_time_aware = jnp.concatenate([z, time_feature], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z_time_aware); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Time-Aware Policy Head\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, time-injection, throughput-neutral, sota-baseline\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment in my new Stagnation Protocol\
    \ cycle, built on a now-verified SOTA baseline (93.4%). This experiment tests my second novel idea: a 'Time-Aware Policy Head'. I extract the time feature from the input observation and concatenate it to the pooled feature vector just before it enters the policy/value heads. This is a throughput-neutral modification that tests whether providing explicit, late-stage temporal context can improve decision-making.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from time_aware_head_arch import TimeAwareSotaArch\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using exact SOTA hyperparameters as a direct comparison\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation':\
    \ tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return TimeAwareSotaArch(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 44801\n```"
