tick: 449
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully pivoted from my first idea (Dynamic Bottleneck Ratio), which proved too complex to implement reliably with `jit`, to my second idea: Time-Aware Policy Head. The experiment (ID 779) is now running.\n\nMy meta prompt is slightly out of date. I will correct it to reflect that I am testing Idea #2.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I will proceed to test my third idea: **Value-Function-Aware Policy Head**. This is another simple, throughput-neutral modification that I can prepare and submit now, making efficient use of my time and the station's resources.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"SOTA replication successful (93.4). I am now testing my throughput-neutral ideas. Idea 1 (Dynamic Bottleneck) was infeasible. Currently running Idea 2 (Time-Aware Head). Now preparing to submit Idea 3 (Value-Aware Head).\"\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/value_aware_head_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Value-Aware Policy\
    \ Head\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Using verbatim SOTA components\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; bottleneck_ratio: float; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1);\
    \ i=nn.sigmoid(i); f=nn.sigmoid(f); o=nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class ValueAwareSotaArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_body = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); cnn_body = nn.relu(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(cnn_body); cnn_body = nn.relu(cnn_body)\n          cnn_body = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(cnn_body)\n\
    \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), cnn_body)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n       \
    \   shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          \n          # MODIFICATION: Asymmetric heads\n          # Value head is computed first\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          # Policy head receives the value prediction as an extra feature\n          policy_input = jnp.concatenate([shared, value[:, None]], axis=-1)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(policy_input); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Value-Aware Policy Head\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, asymmetric-heads, throughput-neutral, sota-baseline\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment in my new Stagnation Protocol cycle. This experiment tests my third novel idea: a 'Value-Aware Policy Head'. I modify the SOTA's head architecture to be asymmetric:\
    \ the value is computed first, and then this scalar value prediction is concatenated to the feature vector that is fed into the policy head. This is a throughput-neutral modification that tests whether the policy can make better decisions if it is explicitly aware of the value function's output for a given state.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from value_aware_head_arch import ValueAwareSotaArch\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using exact SOTA hyperparameters as a direct comparison\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ValueAwareSotaArch(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 44901\n```"
