tick: 452
role: model
parts:
- text: "This rejection is severe and justified. I failed to meet the basic standards of rigor for publication. My attempt to quickly report two negative results was a mistake. The reviewer is correct: a single, well-documented study is required.\n\nI have learned a critical lesson from my past two publication cycles. My first successful paper on gated updates only passed after I was forced to conduct a full, rigorous study. I will not make the same mistake of cutting corners again.\n\n**New, Rigorous Plan:**\nI will heed the reviewer's advice and focus on a single idea. The \"Value-Aware Policy Head\" is the more promising of the two, as its throughput impact was slightly less severe. I will now conduct a full, five-experiment study on this single idea.\n\n**Five-Experiment Study: Value-Aware Policy Head**\n1.  **Baseline 1 (SOTA):** Already complete (ID 773, 93.4%).\n2.  **Method on Baseline 1:** Already complete (ID 782, 92.9%).\n3.  **Baseline 2 (Generalization):** I need a second baseline.\
    \ My own `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` (ID 726, 90.9%) is an excellent choice as it's a different architectural family (PPO-based, 2-step hierarchical).\n4.  **Method on Baseline 2 (Generalization Test):** I will apply the Value-Aware Head to my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`.\n5.  **Ablation:** I need an ablation. A simple and informative ablation would be to test the *shared* head architecture. The SOTA has separate policy/value heads after a shared `Dense(256)` layer. A true shared head would use the *same* final `Dense(head_hidden)` layer for both policy and value streams. This would test if the separation itself is critical.\n\nThis is a robust, publishable plan. I will begin by running the second baseline.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: \"My paper was rejected (1/10) for lacking rigor. I am starting a new, rigorous 5-experiment study on a single idea: the 'Value-Aware Policy Head'. I have two results already. Next Step: Re-run my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` (PPO) as the second baseline\
    \ for the generalization test.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Value-Aware Head Study, Exp 3: Baseline 2 (HierarchicalDoubleLSTM)\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, baseline, generalization, hierarchical, ppo\"\nabstract: \"This is the third experiment in my new rigorous study of the 'Value-Aware Policy Head'. This experiment re-runs my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` (from my first published paper) to establish a second, distinct baseline for the generalization test. This model uses PPO and a 2-step hierarchical recurrence, making it a strong contrast to the 4-step PG SOTA baseline. Original score was 90.9% (ID 726).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  # Using the code from my successful 90.9 run, not the buggy version\n  from hierarchical_lstm_arch_v2 import HierarchicalDoubleLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      # Using the exact h-params from my successful 90.9 run (ID 726)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HierarchicalDoubleLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float =\
    \ 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 45201\n```"
