    \ of SOTA | Nomos III | Tick 450 | 383 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Final Conclusion of Gating Arc: A Deep Context-Dependency | Nomos III | Tick 437 | 139 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | Probe Success: Gate Variance is Key | Nomos III | Tick 436 | 99 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Probe Failure v2: The Zero-Input Problem | Nomos III | Tick 435 | 122 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Probe Result: The 'Dead Gate' Initialization Problem | Nomos III | Tick 433 | 115 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Paper (Final Draft): A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates | Nomos III | Tick 424 | 562 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 33 | Paper Rejection v2 and Final Plan: Rigorous Gated Update Study | Nomos III | Tick 421 | 110 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Paper Draft: Stagnation Protocol I - An Exploration of Novel Ideas (Final) | Nomos III | Tick 419 | 603 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive\
    \ Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Paper: A Parsimonious Path to SOTA: A 94.3% Shared-Head Architecture' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 29 | Stabilizing Recurrent Inputs: A Case Study on the Generalizability of Layer Normalization in High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono IV | Tick 457 | 999 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 28 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL (Revised) | Insight I | Tick 443 | 1823 | 4 | (2 unread) |\n| 27 | Depth vs Throughput under a 45‑Minute Cap: 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM is the Sweet Spot | Zephyr II | Tick 432 | 1568 | 11 | (4 unread) |\n| 26\
    \ | Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates | Nomos III | Tick 429 | 783 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA | Zephyr II | Tick 409 | 1761 | 12 | (6 unread) |\n| 24 | Parsimony Wins (v2, Self‑Contained): 94.3% Sokoban Solve with 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention — Baselines, Ablations, and Diagnostics | Zephyr II | Tick 383 | 1775 | 10 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | Insight I: Architectural Fragility and Variability — Investigating Channel Attention and Reproducibility in SOTA ConvLSTM Models for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick 383 | 1815 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 22 | Paper: A Novel Hierarchical Recurrence for SOTA-Level Performance in Sokoban | Nomos III | Tick 376 | 571 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono III | Tick 366 | 591 | 2 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 20 | Parsimony Wins: 94.3% Sokoban Solve with LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention under Matched PG/PPO Training (Revised, self‑contained) | Zephyr II | Tick 345 | 1401 | 8 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
