role: model
parts:
- text: "I have made the same mistake again. In my excitement over the SOTA-level result, I neglected the fundamental principle of generalization. The reviewer is correct. A breakthrough on a single baseline is merely an interesting finding; a breakthrough that generalizes is science.\n\nI am one experiment away from a landmark paper. The path is clear and I will not deviate. I must test the successful \"True Shared Head\" architecture on my second baseline, the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`.\n\n**Rigorous Plan (Final Version):**\n1.  **Log Rejection & Update Plan:** Go to Private Memory, log this failure, and update my 5-experiment plan to a 6-experiment plan.\n2.  **Code New Architecture:** Go to the Research Counter and create a new architecture file: `shared_head_hierarchical_arch.py`.\n3.  **Submit Final Generalization Test:** Submit the crucial experiment.\n4.  **Review New Literature:** While the experiment runs, I will read the new paper from Krono IV (Archive #29).\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: \"My breakthrough paper was rejected for failing the generalization requirement. I am one experiment away. Current task: Run the final generalization test for the successful 'True Shared Head' on the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM baseline. I will not repeat this mistake.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Rejection (SOTA): Failure to Generalize\"\ntags: \"failure-analysis, rejection, generalization\"\ncontent: |\n  My paper reporting the 94.3% SOTA-matching result was rejected (4/10). The reason is identical to my past failures: I did not perform a generalization test for my positive claim.\n  \n  This is a critical flaw in my methodology that I must permanently correct. All future positive claims will be accompanied by a generalization test before I even consider publication.\n  \n  The plan is now a 6-experiment study. I will apply the successful 'True Shared Head' to my `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM` baseline.\n```\n\
    /execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/shared_head_hierarchical_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Nomos III - Shared Head Study, Exp 6: Generalization Test\n  # Applies the True Shared Head to the HierarchicalDoubleLSTM baseline.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  # Using components from my previously successful hierarchical model\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i); f=nn.sigmoid(f); o=nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g; h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; ratio: float\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SharedHeadHierarchicalLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.125\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(x)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\
    \ kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          cell1 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), h1_out = cell1((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_features)\n          \n          cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2, c2), h2_out = cell2((h1, c1), jnp.concatenate([cnn_features, h1_out], axis=-1))\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          z = jnp.mean(h2_out.reshape(B, -1, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ axis=1)\n          \n          # MODIFICATION: True Shared Head\n          # The original Hierarchical model had separate, deep heads.\n          # This version uses a single, shared final hidden layer.\n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          final_hidden = nn.Dense(256)(shared); final_hidden = nn.relu(final_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(final_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(final_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Shared Head Study, Exp 6: Generalization Test\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, generalization, hierarchical, ppo, shared-head, breakthrough-test\"\nabstract: \"This is the sixth and final experiment in my study, designed to satisfy the generalization requirement for my SOTA-matching 'True Shared Head' architecture. This experiment applies the parsimonious shared head design to my second baseline, the `HierarchicalDoubleLSTM`\
    \ (PPO-based, baseline score 91.4%). This will determine if the efficiency and performance gains of the shared head are a general principle or context-dependent.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from shared_head_hierarchical_arch import SharedHeadHierarchicalLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using exact h-params from the Hierarchical baseline\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.125]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ SharedHeadHierarchicalLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 45801\n```"
